  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>edcc1e17ca77c786f836c5934da14386</srcmd5>
    <version>0.1.13.post2</version>
    <time>1786026184</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-apache-tvm-ffi to 0.1.13.post2.

- post2 keeps object optionals pointer-sized
- post1 marks type-info lookup as pure, makes ModuleObj stable, adds Rust
  structural_visit/structural_walk, and keeps the source patch version ahead of
  post releases

Verified locally on aarch64/openSUSE_Tumbleweed: build green, rpmlint 0 errors
0 badness (the 6 potential-bashisms warnings are in the bundled libbacktrace and
are unchanged from the previous revision), spec-cleaner diff empty,
source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1369641</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>d15a962190ee8a5a5b243501d2fd9975</srcmd5>
    <version>0.1.13.post3</version>
    <time>1786461299</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.1.13.post3: build release wheels for the GIL-enabled CPython 3.14 build (previously only the free-threaded cp314t wheel), and relax the shared-DAG hash scaling threshold in the test suite from 4x to 10x so microsecond-scale timing noise no longer fails it. Built green locally for openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64 (0 rpmlint errors, 0 badness); import smoke test passes for both python313 and python314 flavours.</comment>
    <requestid>1370577</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="6" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>5fdad6633cccf4a271b92e77bb849d87</srcmd5>
    <version>0.1.14</version>
    <time>1789651061</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 0.1.14:
  * Add structural_map, StructuralVisit/Mutate and var_remap APIs,
    with UnchangedOr to skip no-op refcount traffic
  * Make ffi.Error picklable and stabilize Python annotation
    metadata
  * Add a core opaque-pointer handler map for third-party types
    that cannot define __tvm_ffi_opaque_ptr__
  * Publish native layout traits from ObjectDef; stubgen gained
    a --check mode, prefix namespaces and a Rust backend
  * Object::unique() now requires no weak references
  * Support free-threaded Python cross-builds
  * Raise typing-extensions floor to 4.13
- Switch from update-alternatives to libalternatives</comment>
    <requestid>1378289</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
